confirm.description:
{changes}

**Apply all** makes these changes in `{folder}`, then ZHA reloads: your Zigbee devices are unavailable for a few seconds. If a step fails, xquirks tries to put back what it changed before it.

Close this dialog to decide later. **Not now** puts this list aside; a different list comes back as a new repair.

abort.failed_partly:
Stopped at a failure: {failed}

xquirks could not put these changes back:

{left}

ZHA loads what is in `{folder}` now (or at its next start); the next list sets the rest right.

not_applied.description:
{picture}This integration installed `{file}`, but ZHA does not apply it to these devices:

{devices}

A device on another custom quirk: that file wins, remove one of the two. A device on no quirk: ZHA could not load the file, see the Home Assistant log.

misfit.description:
{picture}This collection has `{file}` for these devices, but their endpoints do not fit it, so the integration does not install it for them. A device that runs an older version of the file keeps it until an update for other devices replaces it:

{devices}

Each link opens a prefilled report on GitHub with the device's endpoints and clusters, without its name or address. With it, a later content version puts the clusters where the device has them.

